  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models clearly dominate (0.485–0.520) over image-only (0.208), and among RNA encoders, scvi_n200 (0.520) outperforms pca_n2000 (0.485) in singleprofile rna_only settings. However, scgpt remains untested, leaving uncertainty about which RNA representation is best. Question: config_007 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) provides a clean, single-variable comparison against config_001 (pca) and config_004 (scvi), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and modality constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Resolving the encoder question before investing in multiprofile or multimodal configurations avoids committing the remaining budget to a suboptimal representation. If scgpt is substantially better, it reshapes the entire search; if it is comparable or worse, we can confidently build forward with scvi_n200. This is the highest-information experiment given the current sparse evidence."
